  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want an **info bubble** on Réglages › « Filtrer les posts » that explains what the feature does and what « Minimum de citations » means. Today the section shows a 3/4/5/7/10 picker with no context. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17: « aucune idée de ce à quoi ça sert, je ne dois pas être le seul ».)\n\n### What the feature does, from the code (dev-swift)\n\n« Filtrer les posts » is started from a topic: the topic list's swipe or menu (`Navigation/TopicListView.swift:228`) or the reader's « … » menu (`Reader/ReaderOverflowToolbar.swift:39`). It reads the topic and shows **only the messages that pass at least one rule** (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/FilteredPosts/FilteredPostsCriteria.swift:4-11, 44-53`, a port of legacy `ParseMessagesOperation.m:176-347`):\n\n| Rule | Setting |\n|---|---|\n| The message was **quoted at least N times** (HFR's « Message cité N fois ») | **« Minimum de citations » = N** (3 by default; choices 3, 4, 5, 7, 10) |\n| It is **one of your messages** | — |\n| It **quotes you** (at any depth) | — |\n| It **mentions your pseudo** | — |\n| Its author is on your **liste blanche** | « Inclure les pseudos whitelistés » |\n\nSo a higher N keeps fewer « popular » messages; your own messages and those addressing you are always kept.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. In `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/SettingsView.swift:113-118` (section « Filtrer les posts »), add an `info.circle` button opening a `.popover` (`presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)`), the **same component as #1062 / #1071 / #1065**. Put it on the section header row or on the « Minimum de citations » row, whichever reads better; say which in the PR.\n2. Text: two or three short sentences, built from the verified table. Draft: « Depuis un sujet (menu … › Filtrer les posts), n'affiche que les messages cités au moins N fois, les vôtres, ceux qui vous citent ou vous mentionnent, et ceux de votre liste blanche si l'option est activée. Plus N est grand, moins il reste de messages. »\n3. Accessibility: the button's label is « À propos du filtre des posts ».\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A test that the text exists and names the minimum's role.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nRéglages › Filtrer les posts: (i) explains the feature.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
